1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,179
Chapter 8.

2
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:14,019
I soon learned to know this flower better.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,280
On the little prince's planet the flowers had always been very simple.

4
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:24,139
They had only one ring of petals; they took up no room at all;

5
00:00:24,139 --> 00:00:27,380
they were a trouble to nobody.

6
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:33,920
One morning they would appear in the grass, and by night they would have faded peacefully away.

7
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:42,199
But one day, from a seed blown from no one you were a new flower had come up;

8
00:00:42,199 --> 00:00:46,699
and the little prince had watched very closely over this small sprout which was

9
00:00:46,699 --> 00:00:51,079
not like any other small sprouts on his planet.

10
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:57,820
It might, you see, have been a new kind of baobab

11
00:00:58,519 --> 00:01:04,639
but The shrub soon stopped growing, and began to get ready to produce a flower.

12
00:01:04,639 --> 00:01:09,800
The little prince, who was present at the first appearance of a huge bird felt at

13
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,260
once that some sort of miraculous apparition must emerge from it.

14
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:19,579
But the flower was not satisfied to complete the preparations for her beauty

15
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:22,338
in the shelter of her green chamber.

16
00:01:22,338 --> 00:01:28,820
She chose her colors with the greatest care she dressed herself slowly She

17
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:32,480
adjusted her petals one by one.

18
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:39,880
She did not wish to go out into the world all rumpled, like the field of Poppins

19
00:01:40,639 --> 00:01:47,960
It was only in the full radiance of her beauty that she wished to appear.

20
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,760
Oh, yes!

21
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:58,420
She was a cockettish creature! And her mysterious adornment lasted for days and days.

22
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:08,239
Then one morning, exactly at sunrise, she suddenly showed herself.

23
00:02:08,239 --> 00:02:18,139
And, after working with all this painstaking precision, she yawned and said hmm

24
00:02:18,139 --> 00:02:21,440
I am scarcely awake.

25
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:30,619
I beg that you will excuse me I petals are still all disarranged..."

26
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:37,900
But the little prince could not restrain his admiration: "Oh!

27
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:41,980
How beautiful you are!"

28
00:02:43,338 --> 00:02:45,619
"Am I not?"

29
00:02:45,619 --> 00:02:48,739
the flower responded, sweetly.

30
00:02:48,739 --> 00:02:53,800
"And I was born at the same moment as the sun..."

31
00:02:54,019 --> 00:03:01,219
The little prince could guess easily enough that she was not any too modest-- but how moving--

32
00:03:01,219 --> 00:03:05,500
and exciting-- she was!

33
00:03:06,619 --> 00:03:12,858
"I think it is time for breakfast," she added an instant later.

34
00:03:12,858 --> 00:03:17,059
"If you would have the kindness to think of my needs--"

35
00:03:17,059 --> 00:03:24,139
And the little prince, completely abashed, went to look for a Sprinkling Can of fresh water.

36
00:03:24,139 --> 00:03:26,900
So, he tended the flower.

37
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:32,719
So, too, she began very quickly to torment him with her vanity-- which was, if the

38
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:37,099
truth be known, a little difficult to deal with.

39
00:03:37,099 --> 00:03:44,239
One day, for instance, when she was speaking of her four thorns, she said to the little prince:

40
00:03:44,239 --> 00:03:48,800
"Let the tigers come with their claws!"

41
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:54,079
"There are no tigers on my planet," the little prince objected.

42
00:03:54,079 --> 00:03:58,579
"And, anyway, tigers do not eat weeds."

43
00:03:58,579 --> 00:04:04,579
"I am not a weed," the flower replied, sweetly.

44
00:04:04,579 --> 00:04:06,380
"Please excuse me..."

45
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:15,980
"I am not at all afraid of tigers," she went on, "but I have a horror of giraffes

46
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:20,960
I suppose you wouldn't have a screen for me?"

47
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:28,099
"A horror of drafts-- that is bad luck, for a plant," remarked the little prince,

48
00:04:28,099 --> 00:04:36,699
and added to himself, "This flower is a very complex creature..."

49
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:44,900
"At night I want you to put me under a glass globe it's very cold where you live.

50
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:50,960
In the place where I came from--" But she interrupted herself at that

51
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:54,139
point. She had come in the form of a seed.

52
00:04:54,139 --> 00:04:57,760
She could not have known anything of any of the worlds.

53
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:03,380
Embarrassed over having let herself be caught on the verge of such a naive untruth,

54
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:10,358
she coughed two or three times, in order to put the little prince in the wrong.

55
00:05:11,059 --> 00:05:17,059
"The Scream I was just going to look for it when you spoke to me..."

56
00:05:17,059 --> 00:05:23,900
Then she forced her cough a little more so that he should suffer from remorse just the same.

57
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:30,619
So the little prince, in spite of all the Goodwill that was inseparable from his love,

58
00:05:30,619 --> 00:05:33,320
had soon come to doubt her.

59
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:41,980
He had taken seriously The words, which were without importance, and it made him very unhappy.

60
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:48,739
"I ought not to have listened to her," he confided to me one day

61
00:05:48,739 --> 00:05:52,880
we'll never ought to listen to the flowers. One should simply look at them

62
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:55,579
and breathe their fragrance.

63
00:05:55,579 --> 00:05:59,000
Mine perfumed all my planet.

64
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,960
But I did not know how to take pleasure in all her grace.

65
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:07,579
This tale of claws, which disturbed me so much, should only have filled my heart

66
00:06:07,579 --> 00:06:11,539
with tenderness and pity."

67
00:06:11,539 --> 00:06:19,940
And he continued his confidences: "The fact is that I did not know how to understand anything!

68
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:24,380
I ought to have judged by deeds and not by words.

69
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:32,000
She cast her fragrance and radiance over me I I ought never to have run away from her...

70
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:37,099
I ought to have guessed all the affection that lay behind her poor little stratagems

71
00:06:37,099 --> 00:06:41,358
the Flowers are so inconsistent!

72
00:06:41,358 --> 00:06:47,139
But I was too young to know how to love her
